LICENSE.note for regdatasets
============================

The R code, documentation and package infrastructure of regdatasets are
released under the MIT License (see LICENSE and LICENSE.md).

The datasets come from published studies, textbooks and public data
archives, each with its own terms. This note records, for every dataset,
its original source, how it reached this package, why it may be
redistributed, and how firmly its provenance is established ("verified":
a checkable source ties this exact dataset to its origin; "probable": a
strong match without an explicit statement). Each dataset's help page
summarizes its source and provenance; the full metadata live in
inst/extdata/registry.csv (see list_datasets() for titles and topics).

Most datasets reached this package as teaching extracts used in the
course EDUC 275B (Graduate School of Education, University of California,
Berkeley). This package is not associated with or endorsed by the
original data producers.

Removed in version 1.0.0: `lambert` and `civic_ed`, because no basis for
redistributing them could be established. `naep` was removed in 0.2.0
(restricted-use NCES data).

If you believe a dataset is included in error, please contact the
maintainer listed in DESCRIPTION.

Dataset-level provenance
========================

alcohol1_pp (Adolescent alcohol use (person-period data))
  Source: Singer, J. D., & Willett, J. B. (2003). Applied longitudinal data
  analysis: Modeling change and event occurrence. Oxford University Press.
  Route: Companion data of the book, distributed by UCLA OARC; reached the
  package through the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files.
  Basis: Companion data of a published textbook, freely distributed for
  teaching by UCLA OARC.
  Provenance: verified

berk_sub (Berkeley graduate admissions: two departments)
  Source: Bickel, P. J., Hammel, E. A., & O'Connell, J. W. (1975). Sex bias
  in graduate admissions: Data from Berkeley. Science, 187(4175), 398-404.
  https://doi.org/10.1126/science.187.4175.398
  Route: Subset of berkeley prepared for the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course.
  Basis: Published aggregate admissions table (also in base R as
  datasets::UCBAdmissions), expanded to one row per applicant.
  Provenance: verified

berkeley (Berkeley graduate admissions: five departments)
  Source: Bickel, P. J., Hammel, E. A., & O'Connell, J. W. (1975). Sex bias
  in graduate admissions: Data from Berkeley. Science, 187(4175), 398-404.
  https://doi.org/10.1126/science.187.4175.398
  Route: Via Agresti and Finlay, Statistical Methods for the Social
  Sciences (exercise data), and the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files.
  Basis: Published aggregate admissions table (also in base R as
  datasets::UCBAdmissions), expanded to one row per applicant.
  Provenance: verified

classdata_07 (Simulated class survey)
  Source: Simulated data (regdatasets 1.0.0), modeled on a 2007 class
  survey from the UC Berkeley Graduate School of Education.
  Route: Generated by a seeded simulation in
  data-raw/recipes/classdata_07.R; the original survey is not distributed.
  Basis: Simulated data created for this package; no third-party data are
  included.
  Provenance: verified
  Note: Simulated: the original 2007 class survey has no consent or release
  record.

crime (Florida county crime rates)
  Source: Agresti, A., & Finlay, B. (2009). Statistical methods for the
  social sciences (4th ed.). Pearson Prentice Hall. Florida crime data,
  courtesy of L. Winner, University of Florida.
  Route: Textbook data file (Florida.dat), via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B
  course files; also in the CRAN package smss as fl.crime.
  Basis: Published textbook data of county aggregates, redistributed on
  CRAN (smss).
  Provenance: verified

disc (School discipline: NELS:88 original items)
  Source: National Center for Education Statistics. (1988). National
  Education Longitudinal Study of 1988 (NELS:88), base-year student data
  [Public-use data file]. U.S. Department of Education.
  Route: Teaching extract of 2,000 NELS:88 students prepared for UC
  Berkeley GSE courses (EDUC 293A/275B).
  Basis: NCES public-use data; every NELS variable is in the public-use
  files.
  Provenance: verified
  Note: Same 2,000 students, in the same order, as disc2.

disc2 (School discipline: NELS:88 with SES and test scores)
  Source: National Center for Education Statistics. (1988-1990). National
  Education Longitudinal Study of 1988 (NELS:88), base year and first
  follow-up [Public-use data files]. U.S. Department of Education.
  Route: Teaching extract of 2,000 NELS:88 students prepared for UC
  Berkeley GSE courses (EDUC 293A/275B).
  Basis: NCES public-use data.
  Provenance: verified
  Note: Same 2,000 students, in the same order, as disc.

faculty (Faculty salaries)
  Source: DeMaris, A. (2004). Regression with social data: Modeling
  continuous and limited response variables. Wiley.
  https://doi.org/10.1002/0471677566
  Route: 514-case file of Rabe-Hesketh and Skrondal, Multilevel and
  Longitudinal Modeling Using Stata (Stata Press companion data), via the
  UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files.
  Basis: Published textbook data, publicly redistributed by the publisher
  and Stata Press; contains no names.
  Provenance: verified

gcse (GCSE and London Reading Test scores)
  Source: Goldstein, H., Rasbash, J., Yang, M., Woodhouse, G., Pan, H.,
  Nuttall, D., & Thomas, S. (1993). A multilevel analysis of school
  examination results. Oxford Review of Education, 19(4), 425-433.
  https://doi.org/10.1080/0305498930190401
  Route: The Exam data of the Centre for Multilevel Modelling (Bristol),
  rescaled by 10, via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files; also in the
  CRAN package mlmRev as Exam.
  Basis: Freely downloadable teaching data, redistributed on CRAN (mlmRev)
  and by Stata Press.
  Provenance: verified
  Note: The model-output column pred was removed in 1.0.0.

grades (Essay grades and text features)
  Source: Johnson, V. E., & Albert, J. H. (1999). Ordinal data modeling.
  Springer. https://doi.org/10.1007/b98832
  Route: Extract of essays.dta from Rabe-Hesketh and Skrondal, Multilevel
  and Longitudinal Modeling Using Stata (Stata Press), via the UC Berkeley
  EDUC 275B course files.
  Basis: Published textbook data, publicly redistributed by Stata Press and
  on CRAN (mvord).
  Provenance: probable

gss_1 (General Social Survey 1998)
  Source: Davern, M., Bautista, R., Freese, J., Herd, P., & Morgan, S. L.
  (2026). General Social Survey 1972-2024 [Data file]. NORC at the
  University of Chicago.
  Route: Teaching extract of the 1998 GSS cross-section, of unknown
  authorship, via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files.
  Basis: GSS public-use data, distributed by NORC for research and
  teaching; cited as NORC requires.
  Provenance: probable

hsb_sub (High School and Beyond: five schools)
  Source: Raudenbush, S. W., & Bryk, A. S. (2002). Hierarchical linear
  models: Applications and data analysis methods (2nd ed.). Sage.
  Route: The five lowest-numbered schools of the HSB file, as defined in
  Rabe-Hesketh and Skrondal (Stata Press), via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B
  course files; the full file is also on CRAN (nlme::MathAchieve).
  Basis: NCES public-use survey data, widely redistributed (CRAN nlme,
  mlmRev; Stata Press).
  Provenance: verified

hsbs1 (High School and Beyond: 350 students)
  Source: Tatsuoka, M. M. (1988). Multivariate analysis: Techniques for
  educational and psychological research (2nd ed.). Macmillan.
  Route: 350-student subset of Tatsuoka's 600-student file (also on CRAN as
  candisc::HSB), via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files.
  Basis: NCES public-use survey data printed in a textbook appendix and
  redistributed on CRAN (candisc).
  Provenance: probable

individuals (Earnings, education and job sector (CPS 2000))
  Source: U.S. Census Bureau. (2000). Current Population Survey: Annual
  demographic file, 2000 [Data set]. ICPSR 3048.
  https://doi.org/10.3886/ICPSR03048.v1
  Route: Extract of unknown authorship, via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B
  course files.
  Basis: U.S. federal government data, not subject to copyright (17 U.S.C.
  105).
  Provenance: probable

instruction (Teachers' math knowledge and first-grade math gains)
  Source: West, B. T., Welch, K. B., & Galecki, A. T. (2006). Linear mixed
  models: A practical guide using statistical software. Chapman & Hall/CRC.
  Data from the Study of Instructional Improvement (Hill, Rowan, & Ball,
  2005, American Educational Research Journal, 42(2), 371-406).
  Route: The classroom data of West, Welch and Galecki, as instruction.dta
  in Rabe-Hesketh and Skrondal (Stata Press), via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B
  course files; also on CRAN (WWGbook).
  Basis: Teaching extract publicly released by the book's authors and Stata
  Press, redistributed on CRAN (WWGbook).
  Provenance: verified

nels_data (NELS:88 base year and first follow-up (2,000 students))
  Source: National Center for Education Statistics. National Education
  Longitudinal Study of 1988 (NELS:88): Public-use data files, base year
  (1988) and first follow-up (1990). U.S. Department of Education.
  Route: Teaching extract of 2,000 students prepared for UC Berkeley GSE
  courses (EDUC 293A/275B), about 2004.
  Basis: NCES public-use data: all 296 named NELS variables (plus id, the
  NCES student ID STU_ID) are in the public-use files (checked against the
  NCES variable list).
  Provenance: verified

penalty (Death-penalty verdicts in Florida)
  Source: Radelet, M. L., & Pierce, G. L. (1991). Choosing those who will
  die: Race and the death penalty in Florida. Florida Law Review, 43(1),
  1-34.
  Route: Via Agresti and Finlay (1997), Statistical Methods for the Social
  Sciences (3rd ed., p. 585), and the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files.
  Basis: Published aggregate table, expanded to one row per defendant; also
  on CRAN (catdata, asbio).
  Provenance: verified

pisa2000 (PISA 2000 reading: UK, Germany and USA)
  Source: OECD. (2002). PISA 2000 technical report. OECD Publishing. Data:
  OECD PISA 2000 database.
  Route: Three-country teaching extract made for the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B
  course, with derived variables as in Rabe-Hesketh and Skrondal (Stata
  Press).
  Basis: OECD terms allow copying and distribution with credit to the OECD;
  this package is not endorsed by the OECD.
  Provenance: probable

reading (Reading comprehension experiment)
  Source: Moore, D. S., & McCabe, G. P. (1993). Introduction to the
  practice of statistics (2nd ed., pp. 794-795). W. H. Freeman. Data from
  an experiment by Baumann and Jones (Purdue University).
  Route: Via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files; identical to
  carData::Baumann on CRAN.
  Basis: Published textbook data, redistributed on CRAN (carData, GPL).
  Provenance: verified

satisfaction (Job satisfaction by income and gender)
  Source: Agresti, A. (2002). Categorical data analysis (2nd ed., Table
  7.8). Wiley. Data: 1991 General Social Survey.
  Route: Individual-level expansion of the published table made for the UC
  Berkeley EDUC 275B course; the same table is on CRAN as
  coin::jobsatisfaction.
  Basis: Published aggregate table of counts, redistributed on CRAN (coin).
  Provenance: probable
  Note: Not simulated: one case was added to each of the six empty cells of
  the published table (104 -> 110).

titanic (Titanic passenger survival)
  Source: Cason, T. (1999). titanic3 [Data set]. Department of
  Biostatistics, Vanderbilt University. Based on Encyclopedia Titanica and
  Eaton and Haas (1994), Titanic: Triumph and Tragedy.
  Route: Six of the 14 titanic3 variables, via the UC Berkeley EDUC 275B
  course files; embarked re-taken from titanic3 in 1.0.0.
  Basis: Historical passenger records, publicly distributed by Vanderbilt
  Biostatistics and redistributed on CRAN (carData, PASWR).
  Provenance: verified

womenlf (Canadian women's labour-force participation)
  Source: Fox, J. (2016). Applied regression analysis and generalized
  linear models (3rd ed.). Sage. Data: Social Change in Canada Project,
  York Institute for Social Research (1977).
  Route: Stata Press companion data of Rabe-Hesketh and Skrondal, via the
  UC Berkeley EDUC 275B course files; identical to carData::Womenlf on
  CRAN.
  Basis: Published textbook data, redistributed on CRAN (carData, GPL) and
  by Stata Press.
  Provenance: verified
